# PortableCC Import For ReBSD

This directory contains vendored PortableCC sources imported for the ReBSD
MIPS/N64 system compiler work.

Upstream repositories:

- `pcc`: https://github.com/PortableCC/pcc.git
- `pcc-libs`: https://github.com/PortableCC/pcc-libs.git
- `pcc-tests`: https://github.com/PortableCC/pcc-tests.git

Exact imported commits are recorded in `UPSTREAM-HASHES`.

Local ReBSD patches live on top of these upstream snapshots. The old in-tree
`cc`/`pcc` path remains the compatibility oracle until the new PortableCC-based
pcc passes the full QEMU Malta regression suite.

Porting constraints:

- QEMU Malta is the mandatory test target before N64 hardware testing.
- Existing ReBSD `as`, `ld`, `ar`, and `ranlib` must be used.
- GNU binutils, LLVM tools, a second assembler, a second linker, or a new
  archive format must not be imported as part of this pcc adaptation.
- Kernel and userland builds continue to default to GCC until the pcc port is
  explicitly enabled after tests pass.
